IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`
IMPORT `ei7-related-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23): RELATED PROVISIONS of 2016, c. 7, ss. 225 to 227; 2017, c. 20, ss. 254 to
-- 256; and 2018, c. 27, s. 307 (src:3795-3839 and 3884-3886). 2016, c. 7, ss. 228 and 229 (src:3819-3825) have no rule:
-- they are `inert`. 2018, c. 12, ss. 292 to 295 are in ei7-related-2018-elections.
-- Written by piece ei7 (Sonnet 5.5). Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation
-- current to 2026-09-30; nothing here claims to be verified against the official text.
-- Seat: the person who has lost work or cannot work, asking which version of the Act governs their benefit period.
--
-- Three kinds of section here. (1) "continue to apply, as they read immediately before D": the earlier text of listed
-- provisions governs a benefit period that began before D; the earlier text is not in the deposited texts, so the
-- rule says that it governs and which provisions it governs, not what they say. (2) "apply only ... on or after D":
-- the later text governs from D. (3) a gate on a child's birth or placement, or on a period, before a day.
-- A day fixed by an order of the Governor in Council, or "the day on which ... come into force", is not in the
-- deposited texts: it is a DATE input of the rule that needs it.

§ `2016, c. 7, s. 225 - earlier text that continues to apply`

-- "began before that day and has not ended before that day": the first day is before July 9, 2017 and the last day
-- is that day or later.
-- src:3795 | — 2016, c. 7, s. 225
-- src:3796 | Provisions continue to apply
-- src:3797 | 225 The following provisions of the Employment Insurance Act, as those provisions read immediately before July 9, 2017, continue to apply in respect of a claimant, as defined in subsection 2(1) of that Act, whose benefit period, as defined in that subsection 2(1), began before that day and has not ended before that day:
-- src:3798 | (a) the definition long-tenured worker in subsection 2(1);
-- src:3799 | (b) subsections 10(13.1) to (14.1); and
-- src:3800 | (c) subsections 12(2) to (2.8) and (6).
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2016, c. 7, s. 225 (src:3797)
`Act RP 2016 c. 7 s. 225 July 9, 2017` MEANS YMD 2017 7 9

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2016, c. 7, s. 225 (src:3797)
GIVEN `the benefit period` IS A `Period of days`  -- out of range: section 9 and 10, benefit period (piece ei1); sections 152.1 and 152.11 for a self-employed person (piece ei5)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2016 c. 7 s. 225 the earlier text of the listed provisions continues to apply in respect of the benefit period` IF
        `the benefit period`'s `first day of the period` LESS THAN `Act RP 2016 c. 7 s. 225 July 9, 2017`
    AND `the benefit period`'s `last day of the period` AT LEAST `Act RP 2016 c. 7 s. 225 July 9, 2017`

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2016, c. 7, s. 225 (src:3798-3800)
GIVEN `the benefit period` IS A `Period of days`  -- out of range: section 9 and 10, benefit period (piece ei1); sections 152.1 and 152.11 for a self-employed person (piece ei5)
GIVETH A LIST OF `ei7 Provision of the Act that a transitional section lists`
DECIDE `Act RP 2016 c. 7 s. 225 the provisions whose earlier text continues to apply` IS
    IF `Act RP 2016 c. 7 s. 225 the earlier text of the listed provisions continues to apply in respect of the benefit period` `the benefit period`
    THEN LIST `ei7 s 2(1) the definition long-tenured worker`
            , `ei7 ss 10(13.1) to (14.1)`
            , `ei7 ss 12(2) to (2.8) and (6)`
    ELSE EMPTY

§ `2016, c. 7, s. 226 - later text that applies only from a day`

-- The day is fixed by an order made under subsection 231(3); it is not in the deposited texts.
-- src:3802 | — 2016, c. 7, s. 226
-- src:3803 | Application of provisions
-- src:3804 | 226 The following provisions of the Employment Insurance Act, as enacted by subsections 207(3), 209(1) and 210(1) and (3) and section 220, apply only in respect of a claimant, as defined in subsection 2(1) of that Act, whose benefit period, as defined in that subsection 2(1), begins on or after the day fixed by order of the Governor in Council made under subsection 231(3):
-- src:3805 | (a) subsection 2(5);
-- src:3806 | (b) the portion of subsection 7(2) before paragraph (a);
-- src:3807 | (c) the portion of subsection 7.1(1) before the table and subsection 7.1(3); and
-- src:3808 | (d) subsection 152.07(7).
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2016, c. 7, s. 226 (src:3804)
GIVEN `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE  -- out of range: section 10(1), the day a benefit period begins (piece ei1); section 152.11 for a self-employed person (piece ei5)
      `the day fixed by order of the Governor in Council made under subsection 231(3)` IS A DATE  -- out of range: a day fixed by order or by another section of the amending Act; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2016 c. 7 s. 226 the listed provisions as enacted apply in respect of the benefit period` IF
    `the first day of the benefit period` AT LEAST `the day fixed by order of the Governor in Council made under subsection 231(3)`

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2016, c. 7, s. 226 (src:3805-3808)
GIVEN `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE  -- out of range: section 10(1), the day a benefit period begins (piece ei1); section 152.11 for a self-employed person (piece ei5)
      `the day fixed by order of the Governor in Council made under subsection 231(3)` IS A DATE  -- out of range: a day fixed by order or by another section of the amending Act; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
GIVETH A LIST OF `ei7 Provision of the Act that a transitional section lists`
DECIDE `Act RP 2016 c. 7 s. 226 the provisions that apply as enacted` IS
    IF `Act RP 2016 c. 7 s. 226 the listed provisions as enacted apply in respect of the benefit period` `the first day of the benefit period` `the day fixed by order of the Governor in Council made under subsection 231(3)`
    THEN LIST `ei7 s 2(5)`
            , `ei7 s 7(2) the portion before paragraph (a)`
            , `ei7 s 7.1(1) the portion before the table, and s 7.1(3)`
            , `ei7 s 152.07(7)`
    ELSE EMPTY

§ `2016, c. 7, s. 227 - waiting period provisions that continue to apply`

-- The day is fixed by an order made under subsection 231(4); it is not in the deposited texts.
-- src:3810 | — 2016, c. 7, s. 227
-- src:3811 | Application of provisions
-- src:3812 | 227 The following provisions of the Employment Insurance Act, as those provisions read immediately before the day fixed by order of the Governor in Council made under subsection 231(4), continue to apply in respect of a claimant, as defined in subsection 2(1) of that Act, whose benefit period, as defined in that subsection 2(1), began before that day:
-- src:3813 | (a) the definition waiting period in subsection 6(1);
-- src:3814 | (b) section 13;
-- src:3815 | (c) subsection 22(4);
-- src:3816 | (d) the definition waiting period in subsection 152.01(1); and
-- src:3817 | (e) section 152.15.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2016, c. 7, s. 227 (src:3812)
GIVEN `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE  -- out of range: section 10(1), the day a benefit period begins (piece ei1); section 152.11 for a self-employed person (piece ei5)
      `the day fixed by order of the Governor in Council made under subsection 231(4)` IS A DATE  -- out of range: a day fixed by order or by another section of the amending Act; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2016 c. 7 s. 227 the earlier text of the listed provisions continues to apply in respect of the benefit period` IF
    `the first day of the benefit period` LESS THAN `the day fixed by order of the Governor in Council made under subsection 231(4)`

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2016, c. 7, s. 227 (src:3813-3817)
GIVEN `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE  -- out of range: section 10(1), the day a benefit period begins (piece ei1); section 152.11 for a self-employed person (piece ei5)
      `the day fixed by order of the Governor in Council made under subsection 231(4)` IS A DATE  -- out of range: a day fixed by order or by another section of the amending Act; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
GIVETH A LIST OF `ei7 Provision of the Act that a transitional section lists`
DECIDE `Act RP 2016 c. 7 s. 227 the provisions whose earlier text continues to apply` IS
    IF `Act RP 2016 c. 7 s. 227 the earlier text of the listed provisions continues to apply in respect of the benefit period` `the first day of the benefit period` `the day fixed by order of the Governor in Council made under subsection 231(4)`
    THEN LIST `ei7 s 6(1) the definition waiting period`
            , `ei7 s 13`
            , `ei7 s 22(4)`
            , `ei7 s 152.01(1) the definition waiting period`
            , `ei7 s 152.15`
    ELSE EMPTY

§ `2017, c. 20, ss. 254 to 256 - parental, critically ill child and critically ill adult benefits`

-- s. 254: the earlier Act continues to apply to a claimant for paying benefits under section 23 (Part I) or 152.05
-- (Part VII.1), the parental benefits, for a child born or placed for adoption before the day sections 235 and 245
-- come into force. The Part and the reason are the core's types. For more than one child the day of the first is
-- asked (fork F15).
-- src:3827 | — 2017, c. 20, s. 254
-- src:3828 | Birth or placement for adoption
-- src:3829 | 254 The Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the day on which sections 235 and 245 come into force, continues to apply to a claimant for the purpose of paying benefits under section 23 or 152.05 of that Act in respect of a child or children who are, before that day, born or placed with the claimant for the purpose of adoption.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2017, c. 20, s. 254 (src:3829)
GIVEN `the Part under which the benefits are payable` IS A `Part of the Act`
      `the reason for the benefits` IS A `Reason for benefits`  -- out of range: section 12(3) (piece ei1); section 152.14(1) (piece ei5); the core's Reason for benefits
      `the day on which the child, or the first of the children, was born or placed with the claimant for the purpose of adoption` IS A DATE
      `the day on which sections 235 and 245 of the 2017 Act come into force` IS A DATE  -- out of range: the amending Act's own commencement or royal assent; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2017 c. 20 s. 254 the earlier Act continues to apply to the claimant for paying benefits under section 23 or 152.05` IF
        (   `the Part under which the benefits are payable` EQUALS `Part I`
         OR `the Part under which the benefits are payable` EQUALS `Part VII.1`)
    AND `the reason for the benefits` EQUALS `caring for a new-born or adopted child`
    AND `the day on which the child, or the first of the children, was born or placed with the claimant for the purpose of adoption` LESS THAN `the day on which sections 235 and 245 of the 2017 Act come into force`

-- s. 255: the earlier Act continues to apply for paying benefits under section 23.2 or 152.061 if the period referred
-- to in subsection 23.2(3) or 152.061(3) begins before the day sections 237 and 247 come into force.
-- src:3831 | — 2017, c. 20, s. 255
-- src:3832 | Critically ill child
-- src:3833 | 255 The Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the day on which sections 237 and 247 come into force, continues to apply to a claimant for the purpose of paying benefits under section 23.2 or 152.061 of that Act if the period referred to in subsection 23.2(3) or 152.061(3), as the case may be, of that Act begins before that day.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2017, c. 20, s. 255 (src:3833)
GIVEN `the reason for the benefits` IS A `Reason for benefits`  -- out of range: section 12(3) (piece ei1); section 152.14(1) (piece ei5); the core's Reason for benefits
      `the first day of the period referred to in subsection 23.2(3) or 152.061(3)` IS A DATE  -- out of range: sections 23.2(3) (piece ei1) and 152.061(3) (piece ei5)
      `the day on which sections 237 and 247 of the 2017 Act come into force` IS A DATE  -- out of range: the amending Act's own commencement or royal assent; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2017 c. 20 s. 255 the earlier Act continues to apply to the claimant for paying benefits under section 23.2 or 152.061` IF
        `the reason for the benefits` EQUALS `care or support of a critically ill child`
    AND `the first day of the period referred to in subsection 23.2(3) or 152.061(3)` LESS THAN `the day on which sections 237 and 247 of the 2017 Act come into force`

-- s. 256: sections 23.3 and 152.062 apply to a claimant for any benefit period (a) that begins on or after the day;
-- or (b) that has not ended before that day, but only for weeks of benefits that begin on or after that day.
-- src:3835 | — 2017, c. 20, s. 256
-- src:3836 | Critically ill adult
-- src:3837 | 256 Sections 23.3 and 152.062 of the Employment Insurance Act, as enacted by sections 238 and 248, respectively, apply to a claimant for any benefit period
-- src:3838 | (a) that begins on or after the day on which sections 238 and 248 come into force; or
-- src:3839 | (b) that has not ended before that day, but only for weeks of benefits that begin on or after that day.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2017, c. 20, s. 256 (src:3837-3839)
GIVEN `the benefit period` IS A `Period of days`  -- out of range: section 9 and 10, benefit period (piece ei1); sections 152.1 and 152.11 for a self-employed person (piece ei5)
      `the first day of the week of benefits` IS A DATE
      `the day on which sections 238 and 248 of the 2017 Act come into force` IS A DATE  -- out of range: the amending Act's own commencement or royal assent; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2017 c. 20 s. 256 sections 23.3 and 152.062 apply to the week of benefits` IF
        `the benefit period`'s `first day of the period` AT LEAST `the day on which sections 238 and 248 of the 2017 Act come into force`
    OR  (    `the benefit period`'s `last day of the period` AT LEAST `the day on which sections 238 and 248 of the 2017 Act come into force`
         AND `the first day of the week of benefits` AT LEAST `the day on which sections 238 and 248 of the 2017 Act come into force`)

§ `2018, c. 27, s. 307 - birth or placement for adoption`

-- The same as 2017, c. 20, s. 254, for the day on which section 307 itself comes into force.
-- src:3884 | — 2018, c. 27, s. 307
-- src:3885 | Birth or placement for adoption
-- src:3886 | 307 The Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the day on which this section comes into force, continues to apply to a claimant for the purpose of paying benefits under section 23 or 152.‍05 of that Act in respect of a child or children who are, before that day, born or placed with the claimant for the purpose of adoption.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2018, c. 27, s. 307 (src:3886)
GIVEN `the Part under which the benefits are payable` IS A `Part of the Act`
      `the reason for the benefits` IS A `Reason for benefits`  -- out of range: section 12(3) (piece ei1); section 152.14(1) (piece ei5); the core's Reason for benefits
      `the day on which the child, or the first of the children, was born or placed with the claimant for the purpose of adoption` IS A DATE
      `the day on which section 307 of the 2018 Act comes into force` IS A DATE  -- out of range: the amending Act's own commencement or royal assent; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2018 c. 27 s. 307 the earlier Act continues to apply to the claimant for paying benefits under section 23 or 152.05` IF
        (   `the Part under which the benefits are payable` EQUALS `Part I`
         OR `the Part under which the benefits are payable` EQUALS `Part VII.1`)
    AND `the reason for the benefits` EQUALS `caring for a new-born or adopted child`
    AND `the day on which the child, or the first of the children, was born or placed with the claimant for the purpose of adoption` LESS THAN `the day on which section 307 of the 2018 Act comes into force`
